@startuml Decorator-Middleware-Solution
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
title AFTER — five concerns, five decorators, every order available

interface PriceFeed <<Component>> {
  + quoteFor(sku : String) : Quote
}

class SimulatedRemotePriceFeed <<ConcreteComponent>> {
  + quoteFor(sku : String) : Quote
  + callCount() : int
}

class VendorPriceFeed <<ConcreteComponent, final>> {
  + quoteFor(sku : String) : Quote
}

abstract class PriceFeedDecorator <<Decorator>> {
  - inner : PriceFeed
  + quoteFor(sku : String) : Quote
  # inner() : PriceFeed
}

class LoggingPriceFeed {
  - log : CallLog
  + quoteFor(sku : String) : Quote
}
class TimingPriceFeed {
  - clock : Clock
  - metrics : Metrics
  + quoteFor(sku : String) : Quote
}
class RetryingPriceFeed {
  - maxAttempts : int
  + quoteFor(sku : String) : Quote
}
class CachingPriceFeed {
  - ttl : Duration
  + quoteFor(sku : String) : Quote
  + hits() : int
}
class RateLimitingPriceFeed {
  - limit : int
  - window : Duration
  + quoteFor(sku : String) : Quote
}

PriceFeed <|.. SimulatedRemotePriceFeed
PriceFeed <|.. VendorPriceFeed
PriceFeed <|.. PriceFeedDecorator
PriceFeedDecorator o--> "inner" PriceFeed
PriceFeedDecorator <|-- LoggingPriceFeed
PriceFeedDecorator <|-- TimingPriceFeed
PriceFeedDecorator <|-- RetryingPriceFeed
PriceFeedDecorator <|-- CachingPriceFeed
PriceFeedDecorator <|-- RateLimitingPriceFeed

note right of RetryingPriceFeed
  Forwards **several** times.
end note
note right of CachingPriceFeed
  Forwards **none** on a hit — which
  is why its position in the chain
  matters more than any other's.
end note
note bottom of VendorPriceFeed
  Cannot be subclassed. Is decorated
  anyway: a decorator needs only the
  interface, never the implementation.
end note

note as N1
  **Six classes, all five concerns, every order.**
  A sixth concern is one new class and no edits —
  the open-closed principle stated as an invoice.

  Each decorator is testable alone, because it is
  possible to have exactly one of them.
end note

@enduml
